        {
            'sheet_name': 'Sales_Region_A',
            'value_cell': 'Summary!B5',  # Cell in master sheet with value
            'capture_range': 'A1:G40',   # Range to capture from this sheet
            'embed': True,
            'attach': False,
            'name': 'Region_A_Details'
        },
        # ... more linked sheets
    ]
}

============================================
THRESHOLD TYPES:
============================================

1. 'equals_zero' (=0)
   - Captures sheets where value is exactly 0
   - Use case: Zero inventory, zero sales, empty items

2. 'not_zero' (≠0)
   - Captures sheets where value is anything except 0
   - Use case: Active items, non-empty categories

3. 'exceeds' (>)
   - Captures sheets where value > threshold_value
   - Use case: High sales, excess inventory, budget overruns

4. 'below' (<)
   - Captures sheets where value < threshold_value
   - Use case: Low stock, under budget, declining sales

============================================
REAL-WORLD USE CASES:
============================================

USE CASE 1: Regional Sales Report
- Master sheet shows total sales per region
- Only capture detailed sheets for regions exceeding $10,000 sales
- Threshold: 'exceeds', Value: 10000

USE CASE 2: Inventory Alerts
- Master sheet shows stock levels per warehouse
- Capture only warehouses with zero stock
- Threshold: 'equals_zero', Value: 0

USE CASE 3: Budget Variance Report
- Master sheet shows variance (actual - budget)
- Capture departments over budget (negative variance < -5000)
- Threshold: 'below', Value: -5000

USE CASE 4: Exception Reporting
- Master sheet shows error counts
- Capture only systems with errors (not zero)
- Threshold: 'not_zero', Value: 0

============================================
HOW TO SET UP YOUR FILE:
============================================

1. PREPARE YOUR EXCEL FILE:
   - Create a master/summary sheet
   - Add a column with sum/total values
   - Each value should represent a linked sheet
   - Example: Cell B5 has sum of Sheet "Sales_A"

2. IDENTIFY VALUE CELLS:
   - Note the cell reference for each sum
   - Format: 'SheetName!CellAddress'
   - Example: 'Summary!B5', 'Summary!B6', etc.

3. CONFIGURE IN CODE:
   - Set master_sheet name
   - List all linked sheets
   - Specify value_cell for each linked sheet
   - Set appropriate threshold type and value

4. TEST:
   - Run the application
   - Select the file
   - Capture screenshots
   - Verify correct sheets are captured

============================================
WORKFLOW:
============================================

1. User selects file with smart linking
2. User clicks "Capture Screenshots"
3. System opens Excel file
4. System captures master sheet (always included)
5. System reads value from each value_cell
6. System checks if value meets threshold condition
7. System captures screenshots only for matching sheets
8. User sees list of captured/skipped sheets
9. User drafts email with dynamically selected screenshots

============================================
BENEFITS:
============================================

✅ Automatic sheet selection
✅ Reduces email size (only relevant sheets)
✅ Highlights exceptions/alerts
✅ Saves time (no manual selection)
✅ Consistent logic across reports
✅ Easy to adjust thresholds

============================================
REQUIREMENTS:
============================================

pip install pywin32 pillow pytz

- Windows OS
- Microsoft Outlook installed
- Microsoft Excel installed
- Python 3.6+

